    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 231\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 5719, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the state administrative procedure act, in relation\n      to  the  time  needed by small businesses and local governments to\n      comply with new regulations\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would amend the State Administrative Procedure Act (SAPA) to\nmandate that state agencies:  i)  consider  the  practical,  legal,  and\neconomic  or  fiscal  constraints  that  may affect the ability of small\nbusinesses and local governments to implement  new  regulatory  require-\nments, ii) identify the means by which they intend to communicate policy\nchanges,  and  iii)  require  agencies to engage in targeted outreach to\nactively solicit input from affected entities.\n \n  The ability of small businesses and  local  governments  to  implement\nadopted  regulations is, and always has been, considered during the rule\nmaking process. First,  as  part  of  the  SAPA  process,  agencies  are\nrequired  to analyze the economic and technological impact that proposed\nregulations will have on these  entities.  Second,  SAPA  also  requires\nagencies to list the means by which they intend to afford these entities\nan  opportunity to be heard on policy changes. Third, agencies are mind-\nful that  regulations  cannot  be  implemented  overnight,  and  already\ninclude  additional  time  for  entities  to become compliant before any\nenforcement efforts occur. Finally, this bill would require agencies  to\nprovide notification to every organization that represents the interests\nof affected entities, an impossible task that would require knowledge of\nevery   entity's   business  relationships.  For  these  reasons,  I  am\nconstrained to veto this bill. However, I am directing the Department of\nState to review its existing policies to ensure  that  consideration  is\ngiven  to the needs of small businesses and local governments throughout\nthe SAPA process.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
